  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(446.11pt, 125.9pt, " = 17 to 36 µm) yielded a ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 137.9pt, "minimum overall fanout loss varying from -1.12 to -1.26 dB ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 150.02pt, "(Table II, column 3). In contrast, the doubling of the ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 162.02pt, "waveguide offsets (103 to 153 µm) in Design A increased ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 174.14pt, "losses by ~ 0.4 dB. The micro-mirror reflection and angled ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 186.26pt, "vertical waveguide sections added a further loss of ~ 0.9 dB, ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 198.26pt, "yielding the full chip losses varying from -2.03 to -2.45 dB ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 210.38pt, "(Table II, column 4) over the total of nine circuit designs. ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 222.38pt, "Design C provided the most compact interposer profile, ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 234.5pt, "yielding similar low overall losses to Design B. Only minor ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 246.62pt, "variances in losses were noted in the different waveguide ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 258.65pt, "mappings, offering design flexibility in the channel-to-channel ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 270.77pt, "routing. Designs A-3, B-2, and C-1 (Fig. 3) were selected for ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 282.89pt, "laser fabrication. ")
