  #line-at(46.8pt, 42.48pt, "> REPLACE THIS LINE WITH YOUR MANUSCRIPT ID NUMBER (DOUBLE-CLICK HERE TO EDIT) < ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 65.4pt, "waveguide circuits. The mirror-to-mirror spacing, as small as ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 77.52pt, "50 µm in the present interposer, defines a new approach for ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 89.66pt, "high-density ")
  #line-at(107.984pt, 89.66pt, "3D ")
  #line-at(131.24pt, 89.66pt, "waveguide ")
  #line-at(185.672pt, 89.66pt, "circuitry ")
  #line-at(230.631pt, 89.66pt, "at ")
  #line-at(248.858pt, 89.66pt, "a ")
  #line-at(264.445pt, 89.66pt, "rate ")
  #line-at(290.471pt, 89.66pt, "of ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 101.66pt, "444 mirrors/mm")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(112.22pt, 98.18pt, "3")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(115.46pt, 101.66pt, " that has not previously been applied in fiber ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 113.78pt, "to SiP chip packaging. ")
  #line-at(57pt, 125.9pt, "With the laser propagation on the z-axis (Fig. 1), the present ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 137.9pt, "micro-optic circuit fabrication may be freely extended in the X ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 150.02pt, "and Y directions to scale up the I/O channel count with more ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 162.02pt, "rows of MCF and matching optical circuit layers. This ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 174.14pt, "footprint offers 40 new channels for every millimeter added in ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 186.26pt, "interposer height. Extension of the interposer in the Z ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 198.26pt, "direction would require laying out a more complex network of ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 210.38pt, "TIR etching ports to breach the surface, as well as beam ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 222.38pt, "shaping approaches to compensate the deep-writing effects of ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 234.5pt, "surface aberration [26 Ehsan]. ")
  #line-at(57pt, 246.62pt, "A large component of the -2.75 dB channel loss in the ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 258.65pt, "present interposer (Fig. 6(a)) is due to waveguide propagation ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 270.77pt, "loss (value) which may be improved by further tuning of the ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 282.89pt, "laser beam delivery, for example, by multi-pass writing [29 ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 294.89pt, "AjoyKar] Other compositions of glass, notably Eagle glass [30 ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 307.01pt, "Withford], have demonstrated significantly lower waveguide ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 319.01pt, "propagation loss, but do not offer the 3D FLICE processing ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 331.13pt, "capability for TIR mirror formation. Mirror losses of -0.8 dB ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 343.25pt, "may be addressed by development of a thermal annealing ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 355.25pt, "process [16 Cheng] or alternate etching chemistry. ")
  #line-at(140.54pt, 391.49pt, "V.")
  #line-at(152.3pt, 391.49pt, "C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(158.9pt, 391.49pt, "ONCLUSION")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(57pt, 406.97pt, "The full photonic packaging and characterization of the ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 418.97pt, "interposer demonstrated a robust, high-density platform for ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 431.11pt, "vertical coupling into SiP chips. The femtosecond laser ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 443.23pt, "writing process allows for flexibility of mirror arrangements ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 455.23pt, "and waveguide routing, shown by the multiple interposer ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 467.35pt, "designs that were tested. In the end, an optimized design was ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 479.35pt, "selected and fully packaged into a high-density circuit ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 491.47pt, "with -5.0 dB average single-pass loss, exploiting the full 3D ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 503.59pt, "volume of the glass substrate to weave 40 channels from a 2D ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 515.59pt, "MCF array onto a grid of SiP gratings. The continued ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 527.71pt, "development of glass circuits promises improved channel ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 539.71pt, "numbers and further densification of interconnects, impacting ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 551.83pt, "the interconnectivity bottleneck that the integrated optics and ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 563.95pt, "telecommunication industries are facing at this moment. ")
